what: okay-ui-gtk/ — a Scala Native-only sbt project, AGGREGATED ONLY
  WHEN `pkg-config --exists gtk4` answers (so `sbt test` on a box
  without GTK never sees it): @extern bindings to the handful of GTK 4
  calls a level-L renderer needs, a patch Backend built as Dom/Swing
  are (mirror, React.event, paths walk first-child/next-sibling), a
  window over GtkApplication. Test: the law battery when a display is
  available, skipped (and said so) when gtk_init_check fails.

predict: ~250 lines of bindings + backend; the signal callbacks are
  static CFuncPtrs over a global widget→key table; GTK's main thread
  rule means patches are marshalled through g_idle_add.
